@scene chapter_4b_satchel_of_slots

background: green_valley.jpg
music: wisdom_theme.mp3

dialogue:
"The forest opens onto a trade road, and the trade road is a disaster."
"A caravan sits stranded — wagons half-loaded, crates strewn across the verge in no order at all."
"A broad, grizzled man stamps up and down the line, counting on his fingers and swearing at them."

background: quartermaster

npc Quartermaster:
"Nine! No — eight. BAH."
"Every crate in the wrong wagon, every wagon in the wrong place."
"The Blight came through and scrambled my whole manifest. Now the satchels can't remember what sits WHERE."

dialogue:
"He notices you standing there."

npc Quartermaster:
"You. You've got the look of someone the System still talks to. Don't touch anything yet."
"A satchel isn't a HEAP, traveller. It's a LINE — first slot, second slot, third, order kept, always."
"I'll not have a half-taught hero loose in my satchels. Sit. You'll learn a line before you load one."

system skill_learned:
"MODULE UNLOCKED"
"THE SATCHEL OF MANY SLOTS"
"index · negative index · slice · append / pop / len"

dialogue:
"— LESSON I — EVERY SLOT NUMBERED —"
"He upends a satchel. Crates land in a numbered row, a glowing figure floating over each: 0, 1, 2."

npc Quartermaster:
"Slot zero. First crate. Say it back to me — ZERO is FIRST."
"Reach into a slot by its number and the crate is yours. Reach for the wrong number, you get the wrong crate. Simple. And where everyone goes wrong."

interactive: satchel_index

dialogue:
"— LESSON II — FROM THE OTHER END —"
"He taps the last crate in the line."

npc Quartermaster:
"Sometimes you don't care how long the line is. You just want the LAST one."
"Count backward with a minus. Minus one is the last crate. Minus two, the one before. Never have to count the whole satchel again."

interactive: satchel_negative

dialogue:
"— LESSON III — A RUN OF CRATES —"
"He draws two fingers across a stretch of the line, and those crates glow together."

npc Quartermaster:
"Want a whole RUN of them? That's a slice. From here, up to — but not INTO — there."
"The end number's a wall, same as range. Slot you name at the end, you never actually take."

interactive: satchel_slice

dialogue:
"— LESSON IV — LOAD AND UNLOAD —"
"He hefts a fresh crate and drops it onto the end of the line, then yanks one back off."

npc Quartermaster:
"append puts a crate on the END. pop takes the last one back off. len tells you how many you've got."
"That's the whole job, traveller. Everything else is knowing WHICH slot."

interactive: satchel_methods

npc Quartermaster:
"Now. The thing that ends careers. Reach PAST the end of the line and the satchel screams blue murder."
"Three crates means slots zero, one, two. Ask for slot three and it's 'index out of range' and me doing your paperwork for a week."
"Sort these. Learn where the edge IS before you fall off it."

interactive: satchel_sort_bounds

npc Quartermaster:
"Good eye. Now build me the one command every caravan runs a hundred times a day."

interactive: satchel_forge

dialogue:
"— PROVE IT — ONE FOR THE ROAD —"
"He shoves a half-full satchel and a spare crate at you."

npc Quartermaster:
"Load it. Then tell me — without counting on your fingers — how many it holds now."

system system:
"MISSION"
"Append the item to the satchel, then store the count in crate_count."

mission: satchel_pack

background: quartermaster

npc Quartermaster:
"Ha! Loaded and counted, no fingers. Now the fiddly one."

dialogue:
"— COMBINE IT — EVERYTHING BUT THE ENDS —"
"He lays out a satchel where the first crate is a decoy and the last is a wax seal."

npc Quartermaster:
"First crate's a decoy, last one's the seal. I want everything BETWEEN. One slice. No fumbling."

system system:
"MISSION"
"Store in middle the list with the first and last crates removed, using one slice."

mission: satchel_middle

background: green_valley.jpg

dialogue:
"You cut the slice clean — first and last gone, the middle intact."
"The Quartermaster inspects it, sniffs, and finally — grudgingly — nods."

npc Quartermaster:
"...Right. NOW you know a satchel. Zero to the end and back again."

background: quartermaster

npc Quartermaster:
"One last pack before you go. Everything at once — no hints from me."

interactive: satchel_final_recall

npc Quartermaster:
"Append, then reach for the last slot. That's the whole satchel, and it's yours."
"Now get up. The lesson's over and my caravan is still lying in the road."

system level_up:
"CHAPTER COMPLETE"
"The Satchel of Many Slots"
"Mastered: indexing from 0 · negative index · slicing · append / pop / len"

reward:
xp: 75
gold: 40
achievement: EVERY CRATE IN ITS SLOT

next:
chapter_4_quartermasters_caravan
